 running."]}, "overview": "Celeste Maloy, the Republican incumbent, is seeking another term in a Utah district that leans Republican by roughly 21 points. She has raised about $1.6 million and benefits from more than $1.3 million in outside support, while Democratic nominee Kent Udell has raised under $100,000 and reports minimal cash on hand. Two independents, a Libertarian, and a Constitution Party candidate are also on the ballot.\n\nA September poll of likely voters put Maloy ahead 45 to 26, and prediction markets give her roughly 96 to 97 percent odds. The candidates debated several times in early October on public lands, nuclear energy, and affordability, but those exchanges produced no sign the race is tightening. This contest is rated Safe Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -18.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -18.6}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0119, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.016, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0126, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0174, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.005, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0046, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0072, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0063, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0052, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.008, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0067, "margin": -19.0}, 